/**
@mainpage Nane

<strong>A modern C++23 scientific computing library.</strong>

Nane provides small and composable tools for numerical computing while
using Eigen directly for vectors and matrices.

## Example

Consider the initial value problem

@f[
\dot{x}(t) = -t^2x(t),
\qquad
x(0) = 5.3.
@f]

It can be expressed symbolically and solved with Heun's method:

@code{.cpp}
#include <nane/geometry/uniform_grid.hpp>
#include <nane/numerics/ode/one_step.hpp>
#include <nane/symbolic.hpp>

int main()
{
    nane::uniform_grid<1> time_grid({
        {0.0, 2.0, 101},
    });

    const auto [t, x] = nane::symbols<2>();
    const auto derivative = nane::function(-t * t * x);

    const auto problem = nane::ivp(derivative, 5.3);
    [[maybe_unused]] auto solution = nane::heun(problem, time_grid);

    return 0;
}
@endcode

## Design

Numerical algorithms are provided as small, composable free functions.
Lightweight symbolic expressions provide a concise way to define functions
and coupled systems while remaining directly callable by numerical algorithms.

*/
